  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Chevron Usa obligated $339M in federal contract funds in FY2026 to date. Chevron Usa received 85 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4M. Chevron Usa obligations are up 46.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $55.8M in FY21 to $116M in FY22, $180M in FY23, $132M in FY24, $231M in FY25, and $339M in FY26. Petroleum Refineries is the dominant market for Chevron Usa, accounting for $338M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Chevron Usa also recorded $1.1M in Other Warehousing and Storage obligations. All figures reported are contract obligations except where table notes identify award-value totals. Current-year totals are partial fiscal year to date amounts. This overview focuses on obligations and market concentration so contracting officers and industry teams can see where Chevron Usa is currently active and how that activity compares to recent fiscal years.",
